WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.674
While you build a site, you often need to know which template drew

00:00:04.674 --> 00:00:05.848
a part of a page.

00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:08.400
The Debugging settings answer that question.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.534
In this video, you'll turn on shape debug information, read the comments it

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:14.320
adds, and see who can use it.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.796
Orchard Core builds a page from shapes.

00:00:21.796 --> 00:00:26.207
A shape holds the data to display, and what draws it, usually a

00:00:26.207 --> 00:00:28.636
template, is called its binding.

00:00:28.636 --> 00:00:32.982
Shapes sit inside other shapes, so a page is a tree of shapes,

00:00:32.982 --> 00:00:34.900
down to small fragments.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:39.226
A module provides a default template for a shape, and a theme can

00:00:39.226 --> 00:00:40.736
replace it with its own.

00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:44.262
Templates created in the admin can draw shapes too, so it can be

00:00:44.262 --> 00:00:46.830
hard to tell which one drew a part of a page.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.567
Shape debug information answers that question.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:54.933
When it is on, Orchard Core writes two HTML comments around each shape

00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:57.518
that a template or other binding draws.

00:00:57.518 --> 00:01:02.630
A browser does not display comments, so they appear only in the source of the page.

00:01:06.853 --> 00:01:10.512
In the admin menu, open Settings, and then Debugging.

00:01:10.512 --> 00:01:15.783
The Settings module is always enabled, so there is no feature to turn on first.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.320
The page has one option, Write shape debug information, and it is off by default.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:25.699
Its hint says that it wraps rendered shapes in HTML comments, to help

00:01:25.699 --> 00:01:29.610
identify the template or binding that produced each fragment.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.621
Let's check the box and select Save.

00:01:32.621 --> 00:01:38.790
A message reads, Site settings updated successfully, and the change applies to the running site.

00:01:43.022 --> 00:01:45.441
Let's open the home page of the site.

00:01:45.441 --> 00:01:50.222
It looks like any other page, because a browser does not display HTML comments.

00:01:50.682 --> 00:01:54.223
To read the comments, we open the source of the page, which a

00:01:54.223 --> 00:01:57.024
browser offers as the command View page source.

00:01:57.024 --> 00:02:00.987
Orchard Core has written a comment before and after each shape that a

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.942
template or other binding drew.

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:05.985
A start comment begins with shape-start.

00:02:05.985 --> 00:02:08.325
After type, it gives the shape type.

00:02:08.325 --> 00:02:12.727
After bindings, it gives the binding name, an arrow, the template it came

00:02:12.727 --> 00:02:15.402
from, and in brackets the kind of binding.

00:02:15.865 --> 00:02:20.123
Shapes sit inside other shapes, so comments sit inside other comments.

00:02:20.123 --> 00:02:24.549
Each shape ends with a comment that begins with shape-end and repeats the

00:02:24.549 --> 00:02:27.575
type, so you can match every start with its end.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:36.118
The setting applies to the whole site and to every visitor, and the

00:02:36.118 --> 00:02:38.908
comments name the templates of your site.

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:43.954
When you finish, return to Settings, Debugging, clear the box, and select Save.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.707
Let's reload the source of the home page.

00:02:46.707 --> 00:02:49.967
The comments are gone, and the source is as it was before you

00:02:49.967 --> 00:02:51.330
turned the setting on.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:59.434
The Debugging page requires the permission Manage debugging settings.

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:04.014
The permission Manage settings includes it, together with Manage general settings.

00:03:04.014 --> 00:03:08.386
The Administrator role has them by default, and you can grant Manage debugging

00:03:08.386 --> 00:03:10.000
settings to another role.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:16.171
Another option for building a site is Resource Debug Mode, on the General settings page.

00:03:16.171 --> 00:03:21.419
It decides whether scripts and stylesheets load in their debuggable or minified form.

00:03:21.419 --> 00:03:24.360
A separate video covers the General settings.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:30.250
The Debugging page has one option, Write shape debug information.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:34.194
Turn it on while you build, read the comments to find the template

00:03:34.194 --> 00:03:37.755
behind any part of a page, and turn it off when you finish.

00:03:37.755 --> 00:03:39.180
Thanks for watching.

